WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
science. Why is genetic data treated with
a drastically higher level of legal

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.660
and ethical security than standard medical
records?

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.700
Standard health data reflects an
individual's current condition.

4
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.620
Genetic information differs because it
predicts future health outcomes and

5
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.420
because it is shared across a family
lineage.

6
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.440
Exposing one individual's data exposes
their relatives by default.

7
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:30.280
This shared biological inheritance creates
a severe Science genetic

8
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.440
discussion. These strict protections also
serve as a defense against

9
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.020
aggressive direct-to-consumer genetic
testing, which frequently lacks clinical

10
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.680
validity or professional medical
oversight.

11
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.540
A breach of genetic privacy is not a
temporary individual violation.

12
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.380
It is a permanent multi-generational
exposure of a family's biological

13
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.060
destiny, requiring absolute legal defense.
